conquest in battlefield 1942 Titan in  battlefield 2142 rush in Battlefield Bad  Company 2 there are certain game modes  that seem to define each installment of  battlefields to be the experiences that  players gravitate towards and remember  most vividly with another beta of  battlefield hardline now upon us we're  getting our hands on what I think will  be the signature mode for this entry in  the series Hotwire now hear me out  Hotwire is basically conquest with cars  instead of static points around the map  that each team assaults and defends over  the course of the match there are cars  to capture the point and bleed tickets  from the opposing team you need to get  into the car and drive it above a  certain speed when you slow down or stop  no more capture and when the car blows  up it responds quickly this mobility  makes Hotwire different from conquests  in a few key ways first in order to be  gaining points you have to be actively  driving the car  so no more bleeding tickets just because  the other team hasn't bothered to  recapture that deserted point out in the  boondocks and no more lying and wait out  in the boondocks racking up the XP for  holding the point but actually bored out  of your skull because no one's around in  Hotwire you can't rely on the other  teams passivity to keep a point bleeding  tickets is always an active endeavor  second to capture a point from the enemy  team you have to lure them out of the  car or just blow the thing up entirely  the sneaky infiltration the air drop the  vehicle rush the multi squad Normandy  style onslaught and other tried and true  conquest tactics are pretty much out the  window instead you have the car chase in  which you pack into a car with your  buddies hanging out the window and try  to run them down like crazy vigilantes  you have the ambush in which you get to  an elevated position over a central road  and equip a grenade launcher or put down  breaching charges in the road maybe  parking a car to block the road for good  measures you have the helicopter  pursuits the solo maniac run them off  the road attack the straight-up carjack  or the sabotage in which you use the  mechanics nuke it item to plant a car  bomb under the capture  Carr lying wait and then watch your  enemy try to speed away and  ba-ba-ba-boom all of these tactics don't  just require execution they require  anticipation and planning and okay  sometimes you just get lucky and someone  runs up on you but still the  destructibility and mobility of the  capture points to make this mode feel  dynamic and invigorating of course  Hotwire isn't without its downsides or  potential issues there was a match or  two when I was just cruising this one  loop for minutes and minutes totally  killing it on points but kind of wishing  someone would come mess with me  the driving mechanics are pretty solid  but you couldn't really call them  enjoyable in and of themselves  eventually cruised into the danger zone  just to live a little you know it's also  worth noting that I've only played a few  hours of Hotwire and as we all know the  game changes significantly once tons of  people start playing it figuring out  strategies and counters and generally  being really good at stuff it's possible  that folks will figure out how to kill  cars at will or that helicopters will  just rain terror overall from the jet  'less skies but I still think Hotwire  will succeed because conquest never  really had an answer for the nervous  energy that most players bring to the  game for every cool headed sniper or  stalwart lone defender there were entire  squads of dudes just running from point  to point  capturing and then deserting them  because they didn't want to sit still  they wanted to be where the action was  well there's no sitting still in Hotwire  and I think the frenetic Vaughn of  speeding around in mobile capture points  is just the thing for the boisterous  belligerent energies of battlefield  players  one down
 

